# Breadcrumb

Breadcrumbs show the current location in a hierarchy. Pass an ordered `items` array; the final item is rendered as the current page, while earlier items with an `href` are links.

<DocsExample title="Breadcrumb" source={breadcrumbExampleSource} htmlSource={breadcrumbExampleHtmlSource}><BreadcrumbExample /></DocsExample>

## Collapsed levels

Set `dropdown: true` with an `items` array on any ancestor to fold related levels into a menu and keep the trail short. The trigger shows the item label with a trailing chevron.

<DocsExample title="Breadcrumb with a collapsed level" source={breadcrumbDropdownExampleSource} htmlSource={breadcrumbDropdownExampleHtmlSource}><BreadcrumbDropdownExample /></DocsExample>

## Item schema

- `label` identifies an item; `title` is accepted as an alias.
- `id` provides a stable key for the item.
- `href` makes ancestors links; the final item always renders as the current page.
- `dropdown` with a non-empty `items` array renders the item as a menu trigger with a trailing chevron.
- Nested `items` share the [Dropdown](/docs/components/dropdown) item schema, including group labels, separators, submenus, and `href` links.
- `onselect` runs after a menu entry is selected; entries with `href` also navigate.
